invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_word.h
catches: test/lint-p256-wide.sh
reason: the header picks the overflow builtins for every compiler that
  defines __GNUC__, which gcc does as clang does. gcc expands a builtin
  to an add and a jump on the add's carry, a word's, and removes the
  jump only where its if-conversion passes run: at -Og the wide files
  would hold 73 such jumps. Every value stays right and every test
  binary passes, under clang and under gcc. tools/p256-wide-carry.py
  reads the header as gcc reads it and refuses a builtin there.

--- old
#ifdef __clang__
#define P256_WIDE_CARRY P256_WIDE_CARRY_BUILTIN
--- new
#ifdef __GNUC__
#define P256_WIDE_CARRY P256_WIDE_CARRY_BUILTIN
